{
  "sn35.234:0.1": "Linked Discourses 35.234 ",
  "sn35.234:0.2": "18. The Ocean ",
  "sn35.234:0.3": "With Udāyī ",
  "sn35.234:1.1": "At one time the venerables Ānanda and Udāyī were staying near Kosambī in Ghosita’s monastery. ",
  "sn35.234:1.2": "Then in the late afternoon, Venerable Udāyī came out of retreat, went to Venerable Ānanda, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "sn35.234:1.3": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side and said to Ānanda: ",
  "sn35.234:2.1": "“Reverend Ānanda, the Buddha has explained, opened, and revealed in many ways how this body is not-self. ",
  "sn35.234:2.2": "Is it possible to explain consciousness in the same way? To teach, assert, establish, clarify, analyze, and reveal how consciousness is not-self?” ",
  "sn35.234:3.1": "",
  "sn35.234:3.2": "“It is possible, Reverend Udāyī. ",
  "sn35.234:4.1": "Does eye consciousness arise dependent on the eye and sights?” ",
  "sn35.234:4.2": "“Yes, reverend.” ",
  "sn35.234:4.3": "“If the cause and reason that gives rise to eye consciousness were to totally and utterly cease without remainder, would eye consciousness still be found?” ",
  "sn35.234:4.4": "“No, reverend.” ",
  "sn35.234:4.5": "“In this way, too, it can be understood how consciousness is not-self. ",
  "sn35.234:5.1": "Does ear … nose … tongue … body … ",
  "sn35.234:5.2": "",
  "sn35.234:5.3": "",
  "sn35.234:5.4": "",
  "sn35.234:5.5": "",
  "sn35.234:6.1": "mind consciousness ar